  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on preferring the lottery with a higher probability of a favorable outcome, based on probability comparisons. The individual emphasizes the 100% chance of receiving 2400€ in B versus the 99% chance of a positive outcome in A (with 1% chance of 0€). The individual's deliberation directly references the certainty of a favorable outcome, which aligns with the core of the decision reason. Although the individual also mentions the trade-off of potentially forgoing 100€, the primary justification is the higher (in fact, maximal) probability of a guaranteed gain. The information considered (probabilities of winning something) and the justification (preferring certainty) match the decision reason's rule. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

